Protect representation assumptions across construction and observation (@computing-abstraction-exposure: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "../../inquiry/reproducible-computation/software/Functions-modules-and-boundaries.lingua#r_78TTB7C486WRJJGY0W3GR7H1WQ") { r_00CC9AF3F2F10A112C61003F3E
Reuse [Trace mutation and sharing across a collection boundary](Trace-mutation-and-sharing-across-a-collection-boundary.lingua#r_0E243F4674D6A5A66298639599). If an implementation keeps a caller's mutable list as its private representation, a later caller append changes its state without passing through an operation that preserves the invariant. If an observer returns the implementation's mutable list, the same problem occurs in the opposite direction. Protecting only the constructor or only the observer leaves the other route open. A shallow outer copy is not enough when its elements contain shared mutable objects.

The slot study restricts representations and observations to exact integers and tuples of exact integers. Returning TupleSlots' tuple does share an object, but ordinary clients cannot mutate that tuple or its integer members. MaskSlots constructs an increasing tuple from its bits. The from_values interface requires a tuple rather than silently accepting arbitrary iterable callbacks or mutable nested values. Earlier values remain unchanged under the permitted operations. Accepting richer payloads would require a new ownership, copying or immutable-value argument.

Python frozen dataclasses reject ordinary field assignment. They do not make an access-control or hostile-code security boundary: reflective access, object.__setattr__, class modification and deliberate direct-field use can bypass the intended discipline. Underscore names communicate implementation boundaries rather than enforcing them. The representation-independence theorem concerns cooperative clients using the declared interface. `eq=False` and `repr=False` avoid automatically publishing field-based equality or rendering; object identity and default object rendering still exist outside that interface.

**Bounded source reconstruction:** the inspected MIT reading interprets the character string `acgg` as two inclusive endpoint pairs, giving {a,b,c,g}. Interpreting those same characters as listed members instead gives {a,c,g}. Its range invariant also needs even length and ordered endpoints; an odd-length value has no meaning under that rule. Our original `range_meaning` function reconstructs this example within lowercase ASCII and rejects malformed endpoints. It is not a copied course implementation or a complete Unicode range type. The difference between these interpretations demonstrates why a storage type alone cannot specify meaning.

An invariant can move a recurring precondition into an implementation boundary. The earlier prepared catalog required callers to preserve sorted data. A carefully constructed immutable catalog object could own that obligation, but merely wrapping the data in a class would not prove it. Here the constructors and operations explicitly establish and preserve the slot invariants. Runtime checks diagnose violations; the representation argument explains why ordinary valid operations preserve them.

**Work:** exhibit construction-side and return-side aliasing counterexamples, then repair both under a stated element-type restriction. Reconstruct the selected source example independently and contrast it with direct character membership. Explain why sorted endpoints, even length, the chosen alphabet and the interpretation are separate obligations. Continue through the shared module-boundary lesson; it supplies the application organization rather than duplicating that formation.

